//@version=6
// BTC ATTACK 40 - ATTACK 37 + ONE FILTER: MAXIMUM SWEEP DEPTH (THE MIRROR OF ATTACK 39).
//
// QUEUE ITEM 1, filter-stack term 3 on Attack 37 (37a 1.02423271/322 trades, 37b 1.01155847/196).
// Attack 38 (EMA200 trend gate) was REJECTED for helping H1 and breaking H2, culling ~80% of the
// sample. Attack 39 (minimum sweep depth, floor at 0.15%) was REJECTED on H1 alone: it kept the
// DEEP sweeps (sweepDepth >= 0.15%) and removed the shallow ones, and profit factor FELL (1.024 ->
// 0.982) while net return fell +5.60% -> -3.61%. The direction inverted Attack 37's own stated
// premise: SHALLOW sweeps are the profitable ones, DEEP sweeps are worse.
//
// THIS IS THE PRE-REGISTERED MIRROR, RECORDED IN THE ATTACK 39 QUEUE BEFORE THIS RUN: cap the sweep
// depth instead of flooring it -- require sweepDepth <= maxDepthPct. Attack 39's finding predicts
// this should help, because it keeps exactly the population (shallow sweeps) that Attack 39 showed
// was carrying the return.
//
// WHY THE CAP IS NOT SET TO THE SAME NUMBER (0.15%) AS ATTACK 39'S FLOOR. A literal mirror would use
// an identical threshold, but Attack 39 already measured the population split at that value: floor
// >=0.15% kept 280 of 322 trades (87%), so the complement (<0.15%) is only 42 trades (13%) -- a cull
// as severe as Attack 38's ~80%, which the board explicitly does not want repeated for the same
// reshaping reason. Attack 39 was deliberately kept LIGHT (a 13% trim) by design; this term keeps
// that same design goal by choosing a cap well above the observed 0.15% breakpoint: 0.50%, more than
// 3x Attack 39's floor and still meaningfully below the rBig R-floor's 0.8% (so it is a real
// constraint, not a tautology against rBig). This is a reasoned choice, not the untested guess it
// would be without Attack 39's result to calibrate against -- but the exact trade count this removes
// is unmeasured until the run, and is read first per HARD LESSON 12/E17 before the profit-factor
// number is trusted.
//
// REDUNDANCY (E14), stated the same way as Attack 39: sweepDepth is bounded above by rLong (since
// close > swingLow > low), which rBig already floors at 0.8%. A cap below that ceiling is not
// automatically inert, but if this term barely binds, that bound is the first explanation to check.
//
// AUDIT, one line per leg:
//   R >= 0.8% (LESSON 3) - unchanged from Attack 37, enforced by EXCLUSION via rBig, never clamped.
//   Stop beyond STRUCTURE (LESSON 5) - slPx = the sweep bar's own low, the actual flush extreme.
//        Unchanged.
//   Each leg separately (LESSON 6) - LONG ONLY, as Attack 37 is. Per HARD LESSON 34 a short leg is
//        currently untestable on this engine at this sizing, so this is not an omission to fix.
//   BINDING (E17) - the new term is shallowEnough (sweepDepth <= 0.50%). THE TRADE COUNT IS READ
//        FIRST: a cull toward Attack 38's ~80% would mean this term reshapes the sample rather than
//        trims it, exactly the failure mode this design was chosen to avoid.
//   LATCH IN SEQUENCE (LESSON 8) - swingLow is ta.lowest(low, 20)[1], strictly prior bars; the sweep
//        and reclaim are measured on the current bar and the entry fires at its close. Unchanged.
//   CASCADE (HARD LESSON 35) - long build, expect cascadeRatio 1. Verify it, because only then is the
//        reported count a true position count that RATCHET v2 clause 3 can be applied to.
//   SPLIT (clause 4) - BOTH HALVES ARE RUN IN THIS SAME CYCLE, so a >50% count cut is split-tested
//        before any keep decision by construction, not after.
//   SL and TP FIXED AT ENTRY. No trailing, no averaging down, no martingale.
//
// OUTCOMES REGISTERED BEFORE THE RUN (LESSON 17):
//   * PF IMPROVES ON BOTH HALVES, both counts stay >= 30, drawdown does not worsen -> KEEP under
//     RATCHET v2. This confirms Attack 39's finding and becomes the first filter term this lab has
//     kept on a provable sample.
//   * IMPROVES ONE HALF AND HURTS THE OTHER -> REJECTED, NOT AVERAGED, per the mandate and Attack 38's
//     precedent.
//   * EITHER HALF FALLS BELOW ~30 TRADES -> the ratio is a DIRECTION, not a result (LESSON 12), and
//     the term is rejected on sample grounds regardless of what the profit factor says.
//   * COUNT BARELY MOVES -> the term is INERT, most likely because the 0.50% cap sits above where
//     sweepDepth naturally clusters given rBig's 0.8% ceiling -- a finding about the redundancy noted
//     above, not a failure of the hypothesis.
//   * BOTH HALVES CLEAR 1.0 BUT WORSE THAN THIS -> read against Attack 37's own numbers directly, not
//     just against 1.0, since the goal is improvement on the base, not merely staying positive.
strategy("BTC Attack40 sweep-depth cap", overlay=true,
     pyramiding=1, process_orders_on_close=true,
     commission_type=strategy.commission.percent, commission_value=0.05,
     initial_capital=10000,
     default_qty_type=strategy.percent_of_equity, default_qty_value=100,
     margin_long=100, margin_short=100)

lookback    = input.int(20,     "Swing-low lookback, bars -- held at Attack 37")
rr          = input.float(2.0,  "Reward:risk -- held at Attack 37")
minRpct     = input.float(0.80, "Min stop distance as % of price (LESSON 3) -- held at Attack 37")
maxBars     = input.int(192,    "Max bars in trade -- held at Attack 37")
maxDepthPct = input.float(0.50, "THE ONE NEW TERM: max sweep depth below the swing low, % of price")

swingLow = ta.lowest(low, lookback)[1]

sweep   = not na(swingLow) and low < swingLow
reclaim = not na(swingLow) and close > swingLow
setupOn = sweep and reclaim

sweepDepth   = na(swingLow) ? na : (swingLow - low) / close * 100
shallowEnough = not na(sweepDepth) and sweepDepth <= maxDepthPct

minR  = close * minRpct / 100
rLong = close - low
rBig  = rLong >= minR

goLong = setupOn and rBig and shallowEnough

var float slPx   = na
var float tpPx   = na
var int   barsIn = 0

flat = strategy.position_size == 0

if flat and goLong and rLong > 0
    strategy.entry("L", strategy.long)
    slPx   := low
    tpPx   := close + rLong * rr
    barsIn := 0

if strategy.position_size > 0
    strategy.exit("LX", from_entry="L", stop=slPx, limit=tpPx)
    barsIn := barsIn + 1

if barsIn >= maxBars and strategy.position_size != 0
    strategy.close_all()
    barsIn := 0

plot(goLong ? 1 : 0, title="LongSignal")
plot(swingLow,       title="SwingLow")
plot(sweepDepth,     title="SweepDepthPct")
